# Deployment image pins for THIS host, and the record of what is deployed.
#
# On first deployment:  cp deploy/versions.env.example deploy/versions.env
#
# After that the deploy workflow owns deploy/versions.env and rewrites it
# atomically. Do not hand-edit it while a deploy is in flight.
#
# Two kinds of key live here, written at two different times:
#
#   BACKEND_IMAGE / CADDY_IMAGE are what Compose starts. A deploy writes them
#   before `compose up`, because that is where `up` reads them from.
#
#   APP_VERSION is the record. Nothing interpolates it, so a deploy advances
#   it only after the new containers have passed their health check. It names
#   the last version known to have served — never one that failed, or one a
#   cancelled job left half-started.
#
# A deployed host holds digest pins taken from the release manifest, e.g.
#   APP_VERSION=v1.2.3
#   BACKEND_IMAGE=ghcr.io/colinxu2020/bndsphere-backend@sha256:0f3a...
#
# Digests, not tags: that is what makes a deployed version mean one specific
# set of bytes, and what lets the pull verify itself.

# A real version string, not a word like "local": the deploy script validates
# every requested version against the version grammar before acting on it.
APP_VERSION=v0.0.0
BACKEND_IMAGE=bndsphere-backend
CADDY_IMAGE=bndsphere-caddy
